// @run
// @log 3
// @log 7
// @log 12
// @log 3
// @log 30
// ORDER-INDEPENDENCE of the value floor. A generic function that is ALSO direct-called by name
// used to lose its value use depending on statement order: `dadd(1, 2)` BEFORE `applyD(dadd, …)`
// rejected, while the same two lines swapped compiled.
//
// The mechanism was a spelling, not a type. A DIRECT call materializes the instance with an i32
// pin spelled as the hole it was (`parType = -1` — the emitter's default kind, zero new arena
// nodes), which is byte-identical for a call but leaves `fnHasUnannotatedParam` true. A later
// value use hits that instance in the registry and returns early, so the floor rejected a
// function the program itself had already pinned monomorphic. The registry hit now writes the pin
// onto the shared slot when the hit comes from a VALUE use — the pinned name IS the kind the slot
// already lowers at, so the calls through it are unchanged.
function dadd(a, b) { return a + b }
function dpart(a: i32, b) { return a + b }

function applyD(g: (i32, i32) => i32, x: i32, y: i32) { return g(x, y) }

// Direct call FIRST, value use second.
print(dadd(1, 2)) // 3
print(applyD(dadd, 3, 4)) // 7

// The partially annotated twin, same order.
print(dpart(4, 8)) // 12
print(applyD(dpart, 1, 2)) // 3

// A direct call AFTER the value use still resolves through the same slot.
print(applyD(dadd, 10, 20)) // 30
